window.TLI_DATA = {"project": "tli.cloud: English in Cambodia", "projectKey": "tli-english-cambodia", "version": "1.1", "built": "2026-11-05 07:54", "builtISO": "2026-11-05T07:54:21+01:00", "parts": [{"id": "L.0", "title": "Grade 1 English starter course – overview", "order": 0, "goals": ["Describe who the Grade 1 starter course is for and what it assumes.", "Show the lesson template used in every lesson.", "Explain how each lesson works with a teacher and in the self-paced app."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "audience": "teachers, school leaders, app developers", "grade": "1 (age 6–7)", "cefr_target": "Pre-A1 (adapted descriptors)", "moeys_alignment": "to be checked", "updated": "2026-11-05"}, "file": "l0-course-overview.md", "notes": ["<p>No Grade 1 syllabus was mapped out earlier in the project. This course is a first draft written on these assumptions, which Herbert should confirm: (1) English in public schools officially starts around Grade 4, so Grade 1 English is an enrichment subject for private or NGO-supported schools; (2) pupils are Khmer speakers with no English and are only starting to read Khmer; (3) MoEYS alignment is \"to be checked\" – no MoEYS Grade 1 English syllabus is claimed here.</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.0 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "e6f3b78022", "text": "Grade 1 English starter course – overview"}, {"ref": "L.0 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f7340444ea", "text": "Who this course is for"}, {"ref": "L.0 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-1-1", "kind": "list", "h": "6fb5246054", "text": "Pupils: Grade 1, about 6–7 years old, Khmer as first language, no English yet. Setting: private or NGO-supported primary schools, for example schools linked to YWAM Siem Reap. Classes of 30–50 pupils are expected. Level: CEFR Pre-A1, moving towards A1. The can-do statements are adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020) Pre-A1 descriptors and young-learner practice. They are not an official CEFR test. Reading and writing: the focus is listening and speaking. Pupils see written English words next to pictures, but they are not asked to read or write sentences yet."}, {"ref": "L.0 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5f71879c44", "text": "Lesson template"}, {"ref": "L.0 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-2-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "2be0c699fc", "text": "Every lesson has the same parts, so teachers and pupils know what comes next."}, {"ref": "L.0 §2 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-2-2", "kind": "table", "h": "3c144247af", "text": "Step Time What happens Warm-up 5 min Hello song, review of the last lesson Presentation 7 min New words with pictures, gestures and real objects Practice 8 min Choral repetition, then pairs and small groups Game, song or TPR 8 min Total Physical Response: pupils move to show understanding Wrap-up 4 min Quick check, Goodbye song"}, {"ref": "L.0 §2 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.0-2-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "42441ffdc1", "text": "One lesson takes 30–35 minutes . We suggest two lessons a week, with the second lesson of the week used for review and games."}, {"ref": "L.0 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "eacfc03f32", "text": "Teacher mode and app mode"}, {"ref": "L.0 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-3-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "6903c6f849", "text": "Each lesson has two paths that teach the same words and chunks."}, {"ref": "L.0 §3 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-3-2", "kind": "list", "h": "f4bfc3e0a9", "text": "Teacher mode: the teacher leads the class with flashcards, gestures and songs. No electronics are needed. Every lesson lists activities that work with 30–50 pupils and only a board and chalk. App mode (self-paced): a pupil uses a phone or tablet, alone or with a parent. Every screen plays audio first, uses pictures instead of written instructions, and gives instant spoken feedback. Instructions are in Khmer audio; target words are in English audio."}, {"ref": "L.0 §3 ¶3", "anchor": "p-L.0-3-3", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "f4c1e380d6", "text": "The app never asks a Grade 1 pupil to type. Interactions are tap, drag and \"say it\" (record and play back, no automatic scoring at this level)."}, {"ref": "L.0 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "2402ea3632", "text": "Materials"}, {"ref": "L.0 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-4-1", "kind": "list", "h": "b3dce6ade9", "text": "Flashcards (A4 pictures) for every target word; a printable set per lesson. Real classroom objects (pencil, book, bag) and coloured paper. Audio recordings of every word, chunk and song by a clear English speaker, plus Khmer instruction audio. Simple puppet (a sock puppet is enough) used as the \"English friend\" in every lesson."}, {"ref": "L.0 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "0731877aa6", "text": "Assessment approach"}, {"ref": "L.0 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "a368205b07", "text": "Observation, not tests: teachers tick a can-do checklist for each pupil during games and pair work (see the progress checklist part). App: records which items a pupil got right first time and shows the teacher a simple green, yellow or red summary. Each lesson ends with a short picture quiz that can be done orally in class or in the app."}, {"ref": "L.0 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.0-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "8d8c01266b", "text": "The first five lessons"}, {"ref": "L.0 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.0-6-1", "kind": "list", "h": "1d71a2f487", "text": "Hello! – greetings and my name Numbers 1–5 – How old are you? Colours In my classroom My family"}, {"ref": "L.0 §6 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.0-6-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "a16a8397cb", "text": "Then: progress checklist and review quiz."}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"e6f3b78022\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.0-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Grade 1 English starter course – overview</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f7340444ea\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.0-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Who this course is for</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"6fb5246054\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.0-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Pupils:</strong> Grade 1, about 6–7 years old, Khmer as first language, no English yet.</li>\n<li><strong>Setting:</strong> private or NGO-supported primary schools, for example schools linked to YWAM Siem Reap. Classes of 30–50 pupils are expected.</li>\n<li><strong>Level:</strong> CEFR Pre-A1, moving towards A1. The can-do statements are adapted from the CEFR Companion Volume (2020) Pre-A1 descriptors and young-learner practice. They are not an official CEFR test.</li>\n<li><strong>Reading and writing:</strong> the focus is listening and speaking. Pupils see written English words next to pictures, but they are not asked to read or write sentences yet.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5f71879c44\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.0-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Lesson template</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2be0c699fc\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.0-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Every lesson has the same parts, so teachers and pupils know what comes next.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3c144247af\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §2 ¶2\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.0-2-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §2 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §2 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Step</th>\n<th>Time</th>\n<th>What happens</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Warm-up</td>\n<td>5 min</td>\n<td>Hello song, review of the last lesson</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Presentation</td>\n<td>7 min</td>\n<td>New words with pictures, gestures and real objects</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Practice</td>\n<td>8 min</td>\n<td>Choral repetition, then pairs and small groups</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Game, song or TPR</td>\n<td>8 min</td>\n<td>Total Physical Response: pupils move to show understanding</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wrap-up</td>\n<td>4 min</td>\n<td>Quick check, Goodbye song</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"42441ffdc1\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.0 §2 ¶3\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.0-2-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §2 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §2 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\">One lesson takes <strong>30–35 minutes</strong>. We suggest two lessons a week, with the second lesson of the week used for review and games.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"eacfc03f32\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.0-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher mode and app mode</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"6903c6f849\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.0-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Each lesson has two paths that teach the same words and chunks.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f4bfc3e0a9\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §3 ¶2\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.0-3-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §3 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §3 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶2</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Teacher mode:</strong> the teacher leads the class with flashcards, gestures and songs. No electronics are needed. Every lesson lists activities that work with 30–50 pupils and only a board and chalk.</li>\n<li><strong>App mode (self-paced):</strong> a pupil uses a phone or tablet, alone or with a parent. Every screen plays audio first, uses pictures instead of written instructions, and gives instant spoken feedback. Instructions are in Khmer audio; target words are in English audio.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f4c1e380d6\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"3\" data-ref=\"L.0 §3 ¶3\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.0-3-3\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §3 ¶3\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §3 ¶3 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶3</button><p data-body=\"1\">The app never asks a Grade 1 pupil to type. Interactions are tap, drag and \"say it\" (record and play back, no automatic scoring at this level).</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2402ea3632\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.0-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Materials</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b3dce6ade9\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.0-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>Flashcards (A4 pictures) for every target word; a printable set per lesson.</li>\n<li>Real classroom objects (pencil, book, bag) and coloured paper.</li>\n<li>Audio recordings of every word, chunk and song by a clear English speaker, plus Khmer instruction audio.</li>\n<li>Simple puppet (a sock puppet is enough) used as the \"English friend\" in every lesson.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0731877aa6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.0-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Assessment approach</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a368205b07\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.0-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Observation, not tests:</strong> teachers tick a can-do checklist for each pupil during games and pair work (see the progress checklist part).</li>\n<li><strong>App:</strong> records which items a pupil got right first time and shows the teacher a simple green, yellow or red summary.</li>\n<li><strong>Each lesson</strong> ends with a short picture quiz that can be done orally in class or in the app.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"8d8c01266b\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.0 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.0-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">The first five lessons</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1d71a2f487\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.0 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.0-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li>Hello! – greetings and my name</li>\n<li>Numbers 1–5 – How old are you?</li>\n<li>Colours</li>\n<li>In my classroom</li>\n<li>My family</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a16a8397cb\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.0 §6 ¶2\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.0-6-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.0 §6 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.0 §6 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Then: progress checklist and review quiz.</p></div>"}, {"id": "L.1", "title": "Lesson 1: Hello! – greetings and my name", "order": 1, "goals": ["Pupils can greet someone and say goodbye with a simple word (Pre-A1).", "Pupils can say their name with \"I'm …\" (Pre-A1).", "Pupils can answer \"What's your name?\" with their name."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "cefr": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "moeys_alignment": "to be checked", "duration": "30–35 min", "updated": "2026-11-05"}, "file": "l1-hello.md", "notes": ["<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker, especially the most natural classroom word for \"goodbye\" for small children (លាហើយ or ជំរាបលា).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.1 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "400b3a7b02", "text": "Lesson 1: Hello! – greetings and my name"}, {"ref": "L.1 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-0-1", "kind": "figure", "h": "da39a3ee5e", "text": ""}, {"ref": "L.1 §0 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.1-0-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "755830834e", "text": "In this lesson pupils meet the class puppet and learn to say hello, goodbye and their name."}, {"ref": "L.1 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "4b14327f2c", "text": "Can-do objectives"}, {"ref": "L.1 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-1-1", "kind": "list", "h": "189a8e5768", "text": "I can say Hello and Goodbye to my teacher and friends. I can say my name: I'm Dara. I can understand What's your name? when it is asked slowly with a gesture."}, {"ref": "L.1 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.1 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-2-1", "kind": "table", "h": "0128bdd2b7", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea hello សួស្តី he-LOH child waving goodbye លាហើយ good-BYE child waving at a door name ឈ្មោះ naym name tag teacher គ្រូ TEE-cher teacher at the board friend មិត្តភក្តិ frend two children holding hands"}, {"ref": "L.1 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.1 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-3-1", "kind": "list", "h": "3d12034ccf", "text": "Hello! / Hi! Goodbye! / Bye! What's your name? I'm (name)."}, {"ref": "L.1 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "661ee39e5e", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)"}, {"ref": "L.1 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-4-1", "kind": "list", "h": "0f4d966123", "text": "Warm-up (5 min): The teacher waves and says \"Hello!\" to the class until pupils wave back. Introduce the puppet: \"Hello! I'm Teddy.\" Presentation (7 min): Show the flashcards hello, goodbye, teacher, friend. Say each word three times with a gesture. Model \"What's your name? – I'm …\" with the puppet. Practice (8 min): Choral repetition: whole class, then boys, then girls, then rows. Each row passes the puppet: \"What's your name?\" – \"I'm …\". Game (8 min): Hello–Goodbye. Teacher says \"Hello!\", pupils stand and wave. \"Goodbye!\", pupils sit and wave. Speed up. Wrap-up (4 min): Sing a hello/goodbye song. Five pupils say \"I'm …\" to the puppet."}, {"ref": "L.1 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.1 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "2b162ed6cb", "text": "Meet Teddy: the puppet waves; audio \"Hello! I'm Teddy.\" Khmer audio: \"Tap Teddy to say hello.\" Listen and tap: two pictures (waving hello, waving goodbye). Audio \"Hello!\" – the pupil taps the right one. Right: \"Great!\" with a star. Wrong: the right picture wiggles and the word plays again. Say it: the pupil presses the microphone and says \"Hello!\". The app plays it back next to the model. My name: the pupil records \"I'm (name).\" The recording is saved for the parent or teacher to hear. Song: hello song with tap-along actions."}, {"ref": "L.1 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.1 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-6-1", "kind": "list", "h": "9e38f9490f", "text": "Name chain: in rows, each pupil says \"I'm …\" and the next one says \"Hello, (name)!\". Ball toss: a paper ball goes round; the catcher answers \"What's your name?\". Both work with 50 pupils by running them row by row at the same time."}, {"ref": "L.1 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.1 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "200ac12d91", "text": "Need more support: may answer with just their name, or wave and say \"Hello\". Ready for more: ask a friend \"What's your name?\" and introduce them: \"This is Sokha.\""}, {"ref": "L.1 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.1 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-8-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "400206d473", "text": "The teacher walks round during the ball toss and ticks on the checklist: says Hello / Goodbye, says \"I'm …\"."}, {"ref": "L.1 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.1-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.1 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.1-9-1", "kind": "quiz", "h": "ce79f3e58c", "text": "1. 👋 Your friend comes into the class. What do you say? Hello! Goodbye! We say Goodbye when someone leaves. Five! Five is a number. 2. The teacher asks \"What's your name?\". What do you say? I'm six. That answers \"How old are you?\". I'm Dara. Goodbye. Say your name: I'm … 3. 🚪👋 School is over and you go home. What do you say? Hello! We say Hello when we meet. Goodbye! I'm a pencil. That is not a way to say goodbye. Check Try again"}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"400b3a7b02\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.1-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 1: Hello! – greetings and my name</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-figure fl-right\" data-h=\"da39a3ee5e\" data-kind=\"figure\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.1-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><figure class=\"fig fig-right\" data-body=\"1\" data-marker=\"right\"><button aria-label=\"Enlarge image: Two children wave and say Hello\" class=\"img-zoom\" type=\"button\"><img alt=\"Two children wave and say Hello\" data-src=\"images/hello-wave.svg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/images/images/hello-wave.svg\"/></button></figure></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"755830834e\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.1 §0 ¶2\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.1-0-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §0 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §0 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">In this lesson pupils meet the class puppet and learn to say hello, goodbye and their name.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4b14327f2c\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.1-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Can-do objectives</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"189a8e5768\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.1-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can say <strong>Hello</strong> and <strong>Goodbye</strong> to my teacher and friends.</li>\n<li>I can say my name: <strong>I'm Dara.</strong></li>\n<li>I can understand <strong>What's your name?</strong> when it is asked slowly with a gesture.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.1-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0128bdd2b7\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.1-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>hello</td>\n<td>សួស្តី</td>\n<td>he-LOH</td>\n<td>child waving</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>goodbye</td>\n<td>លាហើយ</td>\n<td>good-BYE</td>\n<td>child waving at a door</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>name</td>\n<td>ឈ្មោះ</td>\n<td>naym</td>\n<td>name tag</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>teacher</td>\n<td>គ្រូ</td>\n<td>TEE-cher</td>\n<td>teacher at the board</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>friend</td>\n<td>មិត្តភក្តិ</td>\n<td>frend</td>\n<td>two children holding hands</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.1-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3d12034ccf\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.1-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>Hello! / Hi!</li>\n<li>Goodbye! / Bye!</li>\n<li>What's your name?</li>\n<li>I'm (name).</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"661ee39e5e\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.1-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0f4d966123\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.1-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up (5 min):</strong> The teacher waves and says \"Hello!\" to the class until pupils wave back. Introduce the puppet: \"Hello! I'm Teddy.\"</li>\n<li><strong>Presentation (7 min):</strong> Show the flashcards hello, goodbye, teacher, friend. Say each word three times with a gesture. Model \"What's your name? – I'm …\" with the puppet.</li>\n<li><strong>Practice (8 min):</strong> Choral repetition: whole class, then boys, then girls, then rows. Each row passes the puppet: \"What's your name?\" – \"I'm …\".</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Hello–Goodbye.</em> Teacher says \"Hello!\", pupils stand and wave. \"Goodbye!\", pupils sit and wave. Speed up.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up (4 min):</strong> Sing a hello/goodbye song. Five pupils say \"I'm …\" to the puppet.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.1-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2b162ed6cb\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.1-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Meet Teddy:</strong> the puppet waves; audio \"Hello! I'm Teddy.\" Khmer audio: \"Tap Teddy to say hello.\"</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and tap:</strong> two pictures (waving hello, waving goodbye). Audio \"Hello!\" – the pupil taps the right one. Right: \"Great!\" with a star. Wrong: the right picture wiggles and the word plays again.</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> the pupil presses the microphone and says \"Hello!\". The app plays it back next to the model.</li>\n<li><strong>My name:</strong> the pupil records \"I'm (name).\" The recording is saved for the parent or teacher to hear.</li>\n<li><strong>Song:</strong> hello song with tap-along actions.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.1-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9e38f9490f\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.1-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Name chain:</strong> in rows, each pupil says \"I'm …\" and the next one says \"Hello, (name)!\".</li>\n<li><strong>Ball toss:</strong> a paper ball goes round; the catcher answers \"What's your name?\".</li>\n<li>Both work with 50 pupils by running them row by row at the same time.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.1-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"200ac12d91\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.1-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> may answer with just their name, or wave and say \"Hello\".</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> ask a friend \"What's your name?\" and introduce them: \"This is Sokha.\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.1-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"400206d473\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.1-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">The teacher walks round during the ball toss and ticks on the checklist: says Hello / Goodbye, says \"I'm …\".</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.1 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.1-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"ce79f3e58c\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.1 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.1-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.1 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.1 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> 👋 Your friend comes into the class. What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Goodbye!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">We say Goodbye when someone leaves.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Five!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Five is a number.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> The teacher asks \"What's your name?\". What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm six.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That answers \"How old are you?\".</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm Dara.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Goodbye.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Say your name: I'm …</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 🚪👋 School is over and you go home. What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">We say Hello when we meet.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Goodbye!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm a pencil.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is not a way to say goodbye.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div></div></div>"}, {"id": "L.2", "title": "Lesson 2: Numbers 1–5 – How old are you?", "order": 2, "goals": ["Pupils can count from one to five (Pre-A1).", "Pupils can say their age with \"I'm six\" or \"I'm seven\" (Pre-A1)."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "cefr": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "moeys_alignment": "to be checked", "duration": "30–35 min", "updated": "2026-11-05"}, "file": "l2-numbers.md", "notes": ["<p>Khmer numerals are standard, but the \"sound hint\" spellings should be tested with Khmer-speaking teachers: the \"th\" in three and the final \"v\" in five are hard for Khmer speakers.</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.2 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "80ee4acf65", "text": "Lesson 2: Numbers 1–5 – How old are you?"}, {"ref": "L.2 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-0-1", "kind": "figure", "h": "da39a3ee5e", "text": ""}, {"ref": "L.2 §0 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.2-0-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "295704457c", "text": "Pupils count to five with fingers and objects, and learn to say how old they are. Six and seven are taught as \"age words\" only."}, {"ref": "L.2 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "4b14327f2c", "text": "Can-do objectives"}, {"ref": "L.2 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-1-1", "kind": "list", "h": "2eb7fc4e8c", "text": "I can count from 1 to 5 in English. I can show a number with my fingers when I hear it. I can answer How old are you? with I'm six. or I'm seven."}, {"ref": "L.2 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.2 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-2-1", "kind": "table", "h": "01c58824d1", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea one មួយ wun one mango two ពីរ too two mangoes three បី three three mangoes four បួន for four mangoes five ប្រាំ fiyv five mangoes six ប្រាំមួយ siks birthday cake, six candles seven ប្រាំពីរ SEV-en birthday cake, seven candles"}, {"ref": "L.2 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.2 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-3-1", "kind": "list", "h": "a6676799bc", "text": "One, two, three, four, five. How old are you? – I'm six. / I'm seven. How many? – Three!"}, {"ref": "L.2 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "661ee39e5e", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)"}, {"ref": "L.2 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-4-1", "kind": "list", "h": "ab530a89b2", "text": "Warm-up (5 min): Hello song. Puppet asks five pupils \"What's your name?\". Presentation (7 min): Count fingers 1–5 slowly. Hold up mangoes, stones or pencils and count them together. Practice (8 min): Teacher shows fingers, class shouts the number. Then pupils show fingers in pairs. Game (8 min): Jump and count. Teacher says \"Three!\", pupils jump three times. Then clap, stamp, nod. Wrap-up (4 min): Puppet asks \"How old are you?\" – class answers together, then a few pupils alone. Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.2 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.2 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "aa31e24b1b", "text": "Count with me: mangoes appear one by one with audio \"one, two, three…\". How many?: a picture of three mangoes; the pupil taps 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5. Feedback: \"Yes, three!\" or the mangoes are counted again aloud. Drag: drag four balls into a basket when the audio says \"four\". Say it: record \"I'm six\" (or seven) after a cake with candles. Song: a counting song with finger animation."}, {"ref": "L.2 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.2 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-6-1", "kind": "list", "h": "4ec498c0e5", "text": "Finger flash: whole class, no materials. Number groups: teacher says \"Three!\", pupils make groups of three. Works in a yard with 50 pupils. Chalk dots: pupils come to the board and draw the number of dots the class says."}, {"ref": "L.2 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.2 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "5ba3b3b63a", "text": "Need more support: show fingers only, without speaking. Ready for more: count backwards from five, or count objects for the class."}, {"ref": "L.2 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.2 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-8-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "673818f161", "text": "Teacher shows 1–5 fingers in random order to small groups and ticks who can name them."}, {"ref": "L.2 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.2-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.2 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.2-9-1", "kind": "quiz", "h": "7ca92672dc", "text": "1. 🥭🥭🥭 How many mangoes? two Count again: one, two, three. three five Count again: one, two, three. 2. ✋ How many fingers? four Count again – every finger and the thumb. five one Look again: the whole hand. 3. The puppet asks \"How old are you?\". What do you say? I'm six. I'm Dara. That answers \"What's your name?\". Hello! Say your age: I'm six or I'm seven. Check Try again"}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"80ee4acf65\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.2-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 2: Numbers 1–5 – How old are you?</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-figure fl-full\" data-h=\"da39a3ee5e\" data-kind=\"figure\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.2-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><figure class=\"fig fig-full\" data-body=\"1\" data-marker=\"full\"><button aria-label=\"Enlarge image: Numbers one to five shown as dots\" class=\"img-zoom\" type=\"button\"><img alt=\"Numbers one to five shown as dots\" data-src=\"images/fingers-1-5.svg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/images/images/fingers-1-5.svg\"/></button></figure></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"295704457c\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.2 §0 ¶2\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.2-0-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §0 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §0 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils count to five with fingers and objects, and learn to say how old they are. Six and seven are taught as \"age words\" only.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4b14327f2c\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.2-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Can-do objectives</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"2eb7fc4e8c\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.2-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can count from 1 to 5 in English.</li>\n<li>I can show a number with my fingers when I hear it.</li>\n<li>I can answer <strong>How old are you?</strong> with <strong>I'm six.</strong> or <strong>I'm seven.</strong></li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.2-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"01c58824d1\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.2-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>one</td>\n<td>មួយ</td>\n<td>wun</td>\n<td>one mango</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>two</td>\n<td>ពីរ</td>\n<td>too</td>\n<td>two mangoes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>three</td>\n<td>បី</td>\n<td>three</td>\n<td>three mangoes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>four</td>\n<td>បួន</td>\n<td>for</td>\n<td>four mangoes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>five</td>\n<td>ប្រាំ</td>\n<td>fiyv</td>\n<td>five mangoes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>six</td>\n<td>ប្រាំមួយ</td>\n<td>siks</td>\n<td>birthday cake, six candles</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>seven</td>\n<td>ប្រាំពីរ</td>\n<td>SEV-en</td>\n<td>birthday cake, seven candles</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.2-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a6676799bc\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.2-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>One, two, three, four, five.</li>\n<li>How old are you? – I'm six. / I'm seven.</li>\n<li>How many? – Three!</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"661ee39e5e\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.2-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ab530a89b2\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.2-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up (5 min):</strong> Hello song. Puppet asks five pupils \"What's your name?\".</li>\n<li><strong>Presentation (7 min):</strong> Count fingers 1–5 slowly. Hold up mangoes, stones or pencils and count them together.</li>\n<li><strong>Practice (8 min):</strong> Teacher shows fingers, class shouts the number. Then pupils show fingers in pairs.</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Jump and count.</em> Teacher says \"Three!\", pupils jump three times. Then clap, stamp, nod.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up (4 min):</strong> Puppet asks \"How old are you?\" – class answers together, then a few pupils alone. Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.2-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"aa31e24b1b\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.2-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Count with me:</strong> mangoes appear one by one with audio \"one, two, three…\".</li>\n<li><strong>How many?:</strong> a picture of three mangoes; the pupil taps 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5. Feedback: \"Yes, three!\" or the mangoes are counted again aloud.</li>\n<li><strong>Drag:</strong> drag four balls into a basket when the audio says \"four\".</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> record \"I'm six\" (or seven) after a cake with candles.</li>\n<li><strong>Song:</strong> a counting song with finger animation.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.2-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4ec498c0e5\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.2-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Finger flash:</strong> whole class, no materials.</li>\n<li><strong>Number groups:</strong> teacher says \"Three!\", pupils make groups of three. Works in a yard with 50 pupils.</li>\n<li><strong>Chalk dots:</strong> pupils come to the board and draw the number of dots the class says.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.2-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5ba3b3b63a\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.2-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> show fingers only, without speaking.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> count backwards from five, or count objects for the class.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.2-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"673818f161\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.2-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Teacher shows 1–5 fingers in random order to small groups and ticks who can name them.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.2 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.2-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"7ca92672dc\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.2 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.2-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.2 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.2 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> 🥭🥭🥭 How many mangoes?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">two</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Count again: one, two, three.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">three</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">five</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Count again: one, two, three.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> ✋ How many fingers?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">four</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Count again – every finger and the thumb.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">five</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">one</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again: the whole hand.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> The puppet asks \"How old are you?\". What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm six.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">I'm Dara.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That answers \"What's your name?\".</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Say your age: I'm six or I'm seven.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div></div></div>"}, {"id": "L.3", "title": "Lesson 3: Colours", "order": 3, "goals": ["Pupils can recognise and name four colours (Pre-A1).", "Pupils can point to or touch a colour when they hear it."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "cefr": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "moeys_alignment": "to be checked", "duration": "30–35 min", "updated": "2026-11-05"}, "file": "l3-colours.md", "notes": ["<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker: ខៀវ can mean both blue and green in some everyday speech, so check how teachers explain the difference to young children.</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.3 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "336aa5250e", "text": "Lesson 3: Colours"}, {"ref": "L.3 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-0-1", "kind": "figure", "h": "da39a3ee5e", "text": ""}, {"ref": "L.3 §0 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.3-0-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "c5d265dfb9", "text": "Pupils learn four colours and use them with things they already know: numbers and classroom things."}, {"ref": "L.3 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "4b14327f2c", "text": "Can-do objectives"}, {"ref": "L.3 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-1-1", "kind": "list", "h": "b1fb4dd62d", "text": "I can say four colours: red, blue, yellow, green. I can touch something red, blue, yellow or green when the teacher says it. I can answer What colour is it? with one word."}, {"ref": "L.3 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.3 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-2-1", "kind": "table", "h": "e4031d461f", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea red ក្រហម red red balloon blue ខៀវ bloo blue balloon yellow លឿង YEL-oh yellow balloon green បៃតង green green balloon colour ពណ៌ KUL-er paint box"}, {"ref": "L.3 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.3 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-3-1", "kind": "list", "h": "952b2b086b", "text": "What colour is it? – Red. Touch something blue! Two yellow balloons. (review of numbers)"}, {"ref": "L.3 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "661ee39e5e", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)"}, {"ref": "L.3 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-4-1", "kind": "list", "h": "5bf72c0c01", "text": "Warm-up (5 min): Hello song, finger counting 1–5. Presentation (7 min): Show coloured paper or balloons one by one. Say the word, class repeats. Practice (8 min): Hide a colour card behind your back, show a corner: \"What colour is it?\". Game (8 min): Touch something… \"Touch something red!\" Pupils touch something red on their clothes, bag or in the room. Wrap-up (4 min): Colour song. Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.3 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.3 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "3fa85ee450", "text": "Paint: a white balloon; audio \"red\" and the balloon turns red as the pupil taps it. Listen and tap: four balloons; audio \"Tap blue!\". Right: the balloon pops with a happy sound. Wrong: the word plays again and the right balloon glows. Drag: sort crayons into colour boxes. Say it: a balloon appears; the pupil says the colour and hears the model. Mix: \"Two green balloons\" – tap the right picture."}, {"ref": "L.3 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.3 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-6-1", "kind": "list", "h": "9fe73a2d3f", "text": "Colour corners: coloured paper in four corners; pupils walk to the colour called. In a big class, send one row at a time. Stand up if…: \"Stand up if you have blue!\". Colour on the board: if no coloured chalk, use coloured paper taped to the board."}, {"ref": "L.3 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.3 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "1e3f86ad4a", "text": "Need more support: point to the colour rather than say it. Ready for more: combine number and colour: \"three red pencils\"."}, {"ref": "L.3 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.3 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-8-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "c204f9445f", "text": "Teacher holds up colour cards to groups of five and ticks who names each one."}, {"ref": "L.3 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.3-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.3 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.3-9-1", "kind": "quiz", "h": "83f574d480", "text": "1. 🔴 What colour is it? red blue Blue is like the sky. green Green is like a leaf. 2. 🍌 What colour is a banana? red Look again – bananas are yellow when ripe. purple Bananas are not purple. yellow 3. 🌿 What colour is the leaf? green yellow Look again at the leaf. red Look again at the leaf. Check Try again"}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"336aa5250e\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.3-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 3: Colours</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-figure fl-full\" data-h=\"da39a3ee5e\" data-kind=\"figure\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.3-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><figure class=\"fig fig-full\" data-body=\"1\" data-marker=\"full\"><button aria-label=\"Enlarge image: Four colour balloons: red, blue, yellow, green\" class=\"img-zoom\" type=\"button\"><img alt=\"Four colour balloons: red, blue, yellow, green\" data-src=\"images/colours.svg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/images/images/colours.svg\"/></button></figure></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c5d265dfb9\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.3 §0 ¶2\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.3-0-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §0 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §0 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils learn four colours and use them with things they already know: numbers and classroom things.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4b14327f2c\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.3-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Can-do objectives</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b1fb4dd62d\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.3-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can say four colours: red, blue, yellow, green.</li>\n<li>I can touch something red, blue, yellow or green when the teacher says it.</li>\n<li>I can answer <strong>What colour is it?</strong> with one word.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.3-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"e4031d461f\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.3-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>red</td>\n<td>ក្រហម</td>\n<td>red</td>\n<td>red balloon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>blue</td>\n<td>ខៀវ</td>\n<td>bloo</td>\n<td>blue balloon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>yellow</td>\n<td>លឿង</td>\n<td>YEL-oh</td>\n<td>yellow balloon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>green</td>\n<td>បៃតង</td>\n<td>green</td>\n<td>green balloon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>colour</td>\n<td>ពណ៌</td>\n<td>KUL-er</td>\n<td>paint box</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.3-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"952b2b086b\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.3-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>What colour is it? – Red.</li>\n<li>Touch something blue!</li>\n<li>Two yellow balloons. (review of numbers)</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"661ee39e5e\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.3-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5bf72c0c01\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.3-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up (5 min):</strong> Hello song, finger counting 1–5.</li>\n<li><strong>Presentation (7 min):</strong> Show coloured paper or balloons one by one. Say the word, class repeats.</li>\n<li><strong>Practice (8 min):</strong> Hide a colour card behind your back, show a corner: \"What colour is it?\".</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Touch something…</em> \"Touch something red!\" Pupils touch something red on their clothes, bag or in the room.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up (4 min):</strong> Colour song. Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.3-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3fa85ee450\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.3-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Paint:</strong> a white balloon; audio \"red\" and the balloon turns red as the pupil taps it.</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and tap:</strong> four balloons; audio \"Tap blue!\". Right: the balloon pops with a happy sound. Wrong: the word plays again and the right balloon glows.</li>\n<li><strong>Drag:</strong> sort crayons into colour boxes.</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> a balloon appears; the pupil says the colour and hears the model.</li>\n<li><strong>Mix:</strong> \"Two green balloons\" – tap the right picture.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.3-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9fe73a2d3f\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.3-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Colour corners:</strong> coloured paper in four corners; pupils walk to the colour called. In a big class, send one row at a time.</li>\n<li><strong>Stand up if…:</strong> \"Stand up if you have blue!\".</li>\n<li><strong>Colour on the board:</strong> if no coloured chalk, use coloured paper taped to the board.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.3-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1e3f86ad4a\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.3-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> point to the colour rather than say it.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> combine number and colour: \"three red pencils\".</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.3-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"c204f9445f\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.3-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Teacher holds up colour cards to groups of five and ticks who names each one.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.3 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.3-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"83f574d480\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.3 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.3-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.3 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.3 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> 🔴 What colour is it?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">red</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">blue</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Blue is like the sky.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">green</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Green is like a leaf.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> 🍌 What colour is a banana?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">red</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again – bananas are yellow when ripe.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">purple</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Bananas are not purple.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">yellow</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 🌿 What colour is the leaf?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">green</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">yellow</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again at the leaf.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">red</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again at the leaf.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div></div></div>"}, {"id": "L.4", "title": "Lesson 4: In my classroom", "order": 4, "goals": ["Pupils can name four classroom things (Pre-A1).", "Pupils can follow simple instructions such as \"Show me your pencil\"."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "cefr": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "moeys_alignment": "to be checked", "duration": "30–35 min", "updated": "2026-11-05"}, "file": "l4-classroom.md", "notes": ["<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker: is កាបូប or កាបូបស្ពាយ the usual word children use for a school bag?</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.4 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "01d9d16b9a", "text": "Lesson 4: In my classroom"}, {"ref": "L.4 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-0-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "ae13d24924", "text": "Pupils name the things on their desk and follow short classroom instructions."}, {"ref": "L.4 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "4b14327f2c", "text": "Can-do objectives"}, {"ref": "L.4 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-1-1", "kind": "list", "h": "db32749c88", "text": "I can name a pencil, a book, a bag and a desk. I can follow Show me your pencil! and Open your book! I can say It's a book. about a picture or object."}, {"ref": "L.4 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.4 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-2-1", "kind": "table", "h": "ff398f6c61", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea pencil ខ្មៅដៃ PEN-sil pencil book សៀវភៅ buk book bag កាបូប bag school bag desk តុ desk school desk"}, {"ref": "L.4 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.4 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-3-1", "kind": "list", "h": "0132be20c7", "text": "What's this? – It's a pencil. Show me your book! Open your book. / Close your book. A red pencil. (review of colours)"}, {"ref": "L.4 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "661ee39e5e", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)"}, {"ref": "L.4 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-4-1", "kind": "list", "h": "0d34df7bab", "text": "Warm-up (5 min): Hello song. \"Touch something red / blue\". Presentation (7 min): Hold up a real pencil, book and bag; point to a desk. Say each word with the class. Practice (8 min): \"What's this?\" – class answers \"It's a book.\" Then pairs ask each other with their own things. Game (8 min): Show me! \"Show me your pencil!\" – pupils hold it up. Teacher says (Simon says): only follow when the teacher says \"Teacher says…\". Wrap-up (4 min): Mystery bag: one pupil feels an object in a bag and guesses. Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.4 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.4 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "9d3cb0f8db", "text": "Look and listen: a desk with four things; tapping each one plays its name. Find it: audio \"Where's the bag?\" – the pupil taps the bag. Drag: pack the school bag – drag the book and pencil into the bag when asked. Say it: a picture appears; the pupil says \"It's a pencil.\" and hears the model. Colour mix: \"Tap the blue book.\""}, {"ref": "L.4 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.4 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-6-1", "kind": "list", "h": "bd9ad1845d", "text": "Show me!: every pupil uses their own things, so it works with any class size. Kim's game: four objects on the teacher's desk; take one away; the class says which is gone. Pass the bag: rows pass a bag while singing; when the song stops, the holder names something inside."}, {"ref": "L.4 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.4 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "a98b3228ef", "text": "Need more support: hold up the object instead of saying the word. Ready for more: add a colour and a number: \"Two yellow pencils.\""}, {"ref": "L.4 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.4 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-8-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "11819dde3b", "text": "During Show me! , the teacher ticks who reacts correctly without copying neighbours."}, {"ref": "L.4 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.4-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.4 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.4-9-1", "kind": "quiz", "h": "ff1aacad33", "text": "1. ✏️ What's this? It's a pencil. It's a bag. A bag is for carrying books. It's a desk. A desk is a table for school. 2. 📖 What's this? It's a pencil. Look again – we read it. It's a book. It's red. That is a colour, not a thing. 3. The teacher says \"Open your book!\". What do you do? Close your book. Open is the opposite of close. Open your book. Say goodbye. Do the action: open your book. Check Try again"}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"01d9d16b9a\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.4-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 4: In my classroom</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ae13d24924\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.4-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils name the things on their desk and follow short classroom instructions.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4b14327f2c\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.4-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Can-do objectives</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"db32749c88\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.4-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can name a pencil, a book, a bag and a desk.</li>\n<li>I can follow <strong>Show me your pencil!</strong> and <strong>Open your book!</strong></li>\n<li>I can say <strong>It's a book.</strong> about a picture or object.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.4-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"ff398f6c61\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.4-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>pencil</td>\n<td>ខ្មៅដៃ</td>\n<td>PEN-sil</td>\n<td>pencil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>book</td>\n<td>សៀវភៅ</td>\n<td>buk</td>\n<td>book</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>bag</td>\n<td>កាបូប</td>\n<td>bag</td>\n<td>school bag</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>desk</td>\n<td>តុ</td>\n<td>desk</td>\n<td>school desk</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.4-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0132be20c7\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.4-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>What's this? – It's a pencil.</li>\n<li>Show me your book!</li>\n<li>Open your book. / Close your book.</li>\n<li>A red pencil. (review of colours)</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"661ee39e5e\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.4-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0d34df7bab\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.4-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up (5 min):</strong> Hello song. \"Touch something red / blue\".</li>\n<li><strong>Presentation (7 min):</strong> Hold up a real pencil, book and bag; point to a desk. Say each word with the class.</li>\n<li><strong>Practice (8 min):</strong> \"What's this?\" – class answers \"It's a book.\" Then pairs ask each other with their own things.</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Show me!</em> \"Show me your pencil!\" – pupils hold it up. <em>Teacher says</em> (Simon says): only follow when the teacher says \"Teacher says…\".</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up (4 min):</strong> Mystery bag: one pupil feels an object in a bag and guesses. Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.4-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"9d3cb0f8db\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.4-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Look and listen:</strong> a desk with four things; tapping each one plays its name.</li>\n<li><strong>Find it:</strong> audio \"Where's the bag?\" – the pupil taps the bag.</li>\n<li><strong>Drag:</strong> pack the school bag – drag the book and pencil into the bag when asked.</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> a picture appears; the pupil says \"It's a pencil.\" and hears the model.</li>\n<li><strong>Colour mix:</strong> \"Tap the blue book.\"</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.4-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"bd9ad1845d\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.4-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Show me!:</strong> every pupil uses their own things, so it works with any class size.</li>\n<li><strong>Kim's game:</strong> four objects on the teacher's desk; take one away; the class says which is gone.</li>\n<li><strong>Pass the bag:</strong> rows pass a bag while singing; when the song stops, the holder names something inside.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.4-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"a98b3228ef\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.4-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> hold up the object instead of saying the word.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> add a colour and a number: \"Two yellow pencils.\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.4-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"11819dde3b\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.4-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">During <em>Show me!</em>, the teacher ticks who reacts correctly without copying neighbours.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.4 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.4-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"ff1aacad33\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.4 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.4-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.4 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.4 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> ✏️ What's this?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a pencil.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a bag.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A bag is for carrying books.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a desk.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A desk is a table for school.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> 📖 What's this?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a pencil.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Look again – we read it.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's red.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">That is a colour, not a thing.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> The teacher says \"Open your book!\". What do you do?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Close your book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Open is the opposite of close.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Open your book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Say goodbye.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Do the action: open your book.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div></div></div>"}, {"id": "L.5", "title": "Lesson 5: My family", "order": 5, "goals": ["Pupils can name four family members (Pre-A1).", "Pupils can introduce a family member with \"This is my mother\" (Pre-A1)."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "cefr": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "moeys_alignment": "to be checked", "duration": "30–35 min", "updated": "2026-11-05"}, "file": "l5-family.md", "notes": ["<p>Khmer to be verified by a native speaker. Khmer separates older (បង) and younger (ប្អូន) siblings; English does not. Teachers should explain this once in Khmer. Children also say ម៉ែ / ប៉ា at home – check which words to show. Be sensitive to pupils who do not live with both parents: accept grandmother, aunt and others (add as extra words if needed).</p>\n"], "blocks": [{"ref": "L.5 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "4dd86b95a4", "text": "Lesson 5: My family"}, {"ref": "L.5 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-0-1", "kind": "figure", "h": "da39a3ee5e", "text": ""}, {"ref": "L.5 §0 ¶2", "anchor": "p-L.5-0-2", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "009968bf95", "text": "Pupils talk about the people at home, using a drawing of their own family."}, {"ref": "L.5 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "4b14327f2c", "text": "Can-do objectives"}, {"ref": "L.5 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-1-1", "kind": "list", "h": "1ff3ef0cd5", "text": "I can say mother, father, sister and brother. I can show a picture and say This is my mother. I can understand Who is this? when the teacher points at a picture."}, {"ref": "L.5 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5a2137d2b9", "text": "Target vocabulary"}, {"ref": "L.5 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-2-1", "kind": "table", "h": "d2d2b47da1", "text": "English Khmer Sound hint Picture idea mother ម្ដាយ MUH-ther mother father ឪពុក FAH-ther father sister បងស្រី / ប្អូនស្រី SIS-ter girl brother បងប្រុស / ប្អូនប្រុស BRUH-ther boy family គ្រួសារ FAM-i-lee whole family"}, {"ref": "L.5 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "f137c97e3d", "text": "Target language"}, {"ref": "L.5 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-3-1", "kind": "list", "h": "81323935b7", "text": "Who is this? – This is my mother. I have a sister. My brother is seven. (review of numbers)"}, {"ref": "L.5 §4 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-4-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "661ee39e5e", "text": "Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)"}, {"ref": "L.5 §4 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-4-1", "kind": "list", "h": "0cab20d767", "text": "Warm-up (5 min): Hello song. \"Show me your pencil!\" Presentation (7 min): Draw a simple family on the board, or show the puppet's family. Name each one. Practice (8 min): Point and ask \"Who is this?\". Then pupils draw their own family in their exercise book. Game (8 min): Family finger song: each finger is a family member, sing and wiggle. Wrap-up (4 min): Three pupils show their drawing: \"This is my father.\" Goodbye song."}, {"ref": "L.5 §5 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-5-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "beb8224862", "text": "Self-paced app lesson"}, {"ref": "L.5 §5 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-5-1", "kind": "list", "h": "cbf17430e3", "text": "Meet Teddy's family: tap each person to hear \"This is my mother\" and so on. Listen and tap: \"Tap the brother!\" Build a family: drag figures into a house; each one says its name. Say it: the pupil records \"This is my …\" for each figure. Song: family finger song."}, {"ref": "L.5 §6 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-6-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "07cd9e0db6", "text": "Activities without electronics"}, {"ref": "L.5 §6 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-6-1", "kind": "list", "h": "dc63b052f9", "text": "Draw and tell: paper and pencil only; pairs show drawings to each other. Family line: five pupils act as a family at the front; the class names each one."}, {"ref": "L.5 §7 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-7-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "7f57b36be2", "text": "Differentiation"}, {"ref": "L.5 §7 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-7-1", "kind": "list", "h": "16831d5fa9", "text": "Need more support: point to the picture when the teacher says the word. Ready for more: add age and colour: \"My sister is five. She has a red bag.\""}, {"ref": "L.5 §8 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-8-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "3bd9f3865f", "text": "Quick assessment"}, {"ref": "L.5 §8 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-8-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "35026a9b80", "text": "During Draw and tell , the teacher ticks who can say \"This is my …\" with one family word."}, {"ref": "L.5 §9 ¶0", "anchor": "p-L.5-9-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "25c86f6a92", "text": "Quiz"}, {"ref": "L.5 §9 ¶1", "anchor": "p-L.5-9-1", "kind": "quiz", "h": "6a624a5bc5", "text": "1. 👩 Who is this? (a woman with her child) This is my mother. This is my father. Father is a man. This is my pencil. A pencil is not a person. 2. 👦 A boy in your family is your… sister A sister is a girl. brother mother A mother is a woman. 3. 👨 Who is this? (a man with his child) This is my sister. A sister is a girl. This is my book. A book is not a person. This is my father. Check Try again"}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4dd86b95a4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.5-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Lesson 5: My family</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-figure fl-right\" data-h=\"da39a3ee5e\" data-kind=\"figure\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.5-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><figure class=\"fig fig-right\" data-body=\"1\" data-marker=\"right\"><button aria-label=\"Enlarge image: Stick-figure family: father, mother, brother, sister\" class=\"img-zoom\" type=\"button\"><img alt=\"Stick-figure family: father, mother, brother, sister\" data-src=\"images/family.svg\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/images/images/family.svg\"/></button></figure></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"009968bf95\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"L.5 §0 ¶2\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-L.5-0-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §0 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §0 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶2</button><p data-body=\"1\">Pupils talk about the people at home, using a drawing of their own family.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"4b14327f2c\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.5-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Can-do objectives</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"1ff3ef0cd5\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-L.5-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>I can say mother, father, sister and brother.</li>\n<li>I can show a picture and say <strong>This is my mother.</strong></li>\n<li>I can understand <strong>Who is this?</strong> when the teacher points at a picture.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5a2137d2b9\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.5-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target vocabulary</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"d2d2b47da1\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-L.5-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>English</th>\n<th>Khmer</th>\n<th>Sound hint</th>\n<th>Picture idea</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>mother</td>\n<td>ម្ដាយ</td>\n<td>MUH-ther</td>\n<td>mother</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>father</td>\n<td>ឪពុក</td>\n<td>FAH-ther</td>\n<td>father</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>sister</td>\n<td>បងស្រី / ប្អូនស្រី</td>\n<td>SIS-ter</td>\n<td>girl</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>brother</td>\n<td>បងប្រុស / ប្អូនប្រុស</td>\n<td>BRUH-ther</td>\n<td>boy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>family</td>\n<td>គ្រួសារ</td>\n<td>FAM-i-lee</td>\n<td>whole family</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f137c97e3d\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.5-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Target language</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"81323935b7\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-L.5-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li>Who is this? – This is my mother.</li>\n<li>I have a sister.</li>\n<li>My brother is seven. (review of numbers)</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"661ee39e5e\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §4 ¶0\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.5-4-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §4 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §4 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Teacher-led lesson (30–35 min)</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"0cab20d767\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §4 ¶1\" data-sec=\"4\" id=\"p-L.5-4-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §4 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §4 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§4 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Warm-up (5 min):</strong> Hello song. \"Show me your pencil!\"</li>\n<li><strong>Presentation (7 min):</strong> Draw a simple family on the board, or show the puppet's family. Name each one.</li>\n<li><strong>Practice (8 min):</strong> Point and ask \"Who is this?\". Then pupils draw their own family in their exercise book.</li>\n<li><strong>Game (8 min):</strong> <em>Family finger song:</em> each finger is a family member, sing and wiggle.</li>\n<li><strong>Wrap-up (4 min):</strong> Three pupils show their drawing: \"This is my father.\" Goodbye song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"beb8224862\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §5 ¶0\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.5-5-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §5 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §5 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Self-paced app lesson</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"cbf17430e3\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §5 ¶1\" data-sec=\"5\" id=\"p-L.5-5-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §5 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §5 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§5 ¶1</button><ol data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Meet Teddy's family:</strong> tap each person to hear \"This is my mother\" and so on.</li>\n<li><strong>Listen and tap:</strong> \"Tap the brother!\"</li>\n<li><strong>Build a family:</strong> drag figures into a house; each one says its name.</li>\n<li><strong>Say it:</strong> the pupil records \"This is my …\" for each figure.</li>\n<li><strong>Song:</strong> family finger song.</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"07cd9e0db6\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §6 ¶0\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.5-6-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §6 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §6 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Activities without electronics</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"dc63b052f9\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §6 ¶1\" data-sec=\"6\" id=\"p-L.5-6-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §6 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §6 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§6 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Draw and tell:</strong> paper and pencil only; pairs show drawings to each other.</li>\n<li><strong>Family line:</strong> five pupils act as a family at the front; the class names each one.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"7f57b36be2\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §7 ¶0\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.5-7-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §7 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §7 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Differentiation</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"16831d5fa9\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §7 ¶1\" data-sec=\"7\" id=\"p-L.5-7-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §7 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §7 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§7 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Need more support:</strong> point to the picture when the teacher says the word.</li>\n<li><strong>Ready for more:</strong> add age and colour: \"My sister is five. She has a red bag.\"</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"3bd9f3865f\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §8 ¶0\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.5-8-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §8 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §8 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quick assessment</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"35026a9b80\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §8 ¶1\" data-sec=\"8\" id=\"p-L.5-8-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §8 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §8 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§8 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">During <em>Draw and tell</em>, the teacher ticks who can say \"This is my …\" with one family word.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"25c86f6a92\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"L.5 §9 ¶0\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.5-9-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §9 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §9 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"6a624a5bc5\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"L.5 §9 ¶1\" data-sec=\"9\" id=\"p-L.5-9-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference L.5 §9 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"L.5 §9 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§9 ¶1</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> 👩 Who is this? (a woman with her child)</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my mother.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my father.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Father is a man.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my pencil.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A pencil is not a person.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> 👦 A boy in your family is your…</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">sister</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A sister is a girl.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">brother</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">mother</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A mother is a woman.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 👨 Who is this? (a man with his child)</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my sister.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A sister is a girl.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A book is not a person.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">This is my father.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div></div></div>"}, {"id": "R.1", "title": "Progress checklist and review quiz (Lessons 1–5)", "order": 6, "goals": ["Give teachers one checklist to record each pupil's progress after Lessons 1–5.", "Review all five lessons with one quiz."], "metadata": {"status": "draft", "grade": "1", "cefr": "Pre-A1 (adapted, CEFR Companion Volume)", "moeys_alignment": "to be checked", "updated": "2026-11-05"}, "file": "r1-progress-checklist.md", "notes": [], "blocks": [{"ref": "R.1 §0 ¶0", "anchor": "p-R.1-0-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "8700d44294", "text": "Progress checklist and review quiz (Lessons 1–5)"}, {"ref": "R.1 §0 ¶1", "anchor": "p-R.1-0-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "88375ea4be", "text": "Use this checklist after Lesson 5. Watch pupils during games and pair work; do not give a written test."}, {"ref": "R.1 §1 ¶0", "anchor": "p-R.1-1-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5b0974c067", "text": "Can-do checklist"}, {"ref": "R.1 §1 ¶1", "anchor": "p-R.1-1-1", "kind": "paragraph", "h": "b6272d594d", "text": "Example record for one pupil. Use green for \"can do alone\", yellow for \"can do with help\" and red for \"not yet\"."}, {"ref": "R.1 §1 ¶2", "anchor": "p-R.1-1-2", "kind": "table", "h": "f72bdedd7c", "text": "Can-do statement Lesson Example pupil I can say Hello and Goodbye. 1 yes (rated green) I can say my name: I'm … 1 yes (rated green) I can count from 1 to 5. 2 with help (rated yellow) I can say how old I am. 2 yes (rated green) I can name four colours. 3 with help (rated yellow) I can name a pencil, a book, a bag and a desk. 4 not yet (rated red) I can follow \"Show me your …!\". 4 yes (rated green) I can say \"This is my mother / father / sister / brother\". 5 with help (rated yellow)"}, {"ref": "R.1 §2 ¶0", "anchor": "p-R.1-2-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "5089e26de4", "text": "What to do with the results"}, {"ref": "R.1 §2 ¶1", "anchor": "p-R.1-2-1", "kind": "list", "h": "10a21a9a84", "text": "Mostly green: go on to the next unit. Some yellow: repeat the games from those lessons in the review lesson. Red: give the pupil a partner who is green, and use the app at home if possible."}, {"ref": "R.1 §3 ¶0", "anchor": "p-R.1-3-0", "kind": "heading", "h": "bed7b0b1ee", "text": "Review quiz"}, {"ref": "R.1 §3 ¶1", "anchor": "p-R.1-3-1", "kind": "quiz", "h": "de5058e914", "text": "1. You meet your teacher in the morning. What do you say? Hello! Goodbye! Goodbye is for when you leave. Four! Four is a number. 2. 🖐️ How many fingers? three Count again: one, two, three, four, five. four Count again – do not forget the thumb. five 3. 🟦 What colour is it? yellow Yellow is like a banana. blue red Red is like a chilli. 4. 🎒 What's this? It's a bag. It's a desk. A desk is a table. It's a book. A book has pages. 5. 👧 A girl in your family is your… brother A brother is a boy. sister father A father is a man. Check Try again"}], "html": "<div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"8700d44294\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"R.1 §0 ¶0\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-R.1-0-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §0 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §0 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶0</button><h1 data-body=\"1\">Progress checklist and review quiz (Lessons 1–5)</h1></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"88375ea4be\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"R.1 §0 ¶1\" data-sec=\"0\" id=\"p-R.1-0-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §0 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §0 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§0 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Use this checklist after Lesson 5. Watch pupils during games and pair work; do not give a written test.</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5b0974c067\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"R.1 §1 ¶0\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-R.1-1-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §1 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §1 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Can-do checklist</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-paragraph\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"b6272d594d\" data-kind=\"paragraph\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"R.1 §1 ¶1\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-R.1-1-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §1 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §1 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶1</button><p data-body=\"1\">Example record for one pupil. Use <strong>green</strong> for \"can do alone\", <strong>yellow</strong> for \"can do with help\" and <strong>red</strong> for \"not yet\".</p></div><div class=\"blk blk-table\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"f72bdedd7c\" data-kind=\"table\" data-par=\"2\" data-ref=\"R.1 §1 ¶2\" data-sec=\"1\" id=\"p-R.1-1-2\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §1 ¶2\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §1 ¶2 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§1 ¶2</button><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\" data-body=\"1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Can-do statement</th>\n<th>Lesson</th>\n<th>Example pupil</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>I can say Hello and Goodbye.</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">yes<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I can say my name: I'm …</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">yes<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I can count from 1 to 5.</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I can say how old I am.</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">yes<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I can name four colours.</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I can name a pencil, a book, a bag and a desk.</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td class=\"cell-red\">not yet<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"red\" title=\"Rated red\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-xmark\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated red)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I can follow \"Show me your …!\".</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td class=\"cell-green\">yes<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"green\" title=\"Rated green\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-check\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated green)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>I can say \"This is my mother / father / sister / brother\".</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td class=\"cell-yellow\">with help<span class=\"cell-tag\" data-tag=\"yellow\" title=\"Rated yellow\"> <i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation\"></i><span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (rated yellow)</span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"5089e26de4\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"R.1 §2 ¶0\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-R.1-2-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §2 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §2 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">What to do with the results</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-list\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"10a21a9a84\" data-kind=\"list\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"R.1 §2 ¶1\" data-sec=\"2\" id=\"p-R.1-2-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §2 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §2 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§2 ¶1</button><ul data-body=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Mostly green:</strong> go on to the next unit.</li>\n<li><strong>Some yellow:</strong> repeat the games from those lessons in the review lesson.</li>\n<li><strong>Red:</strong> give the pupil a partner who is green, and use the app at home if possible.</li>\n</ul></div><div class=\"blk blk-heading\" data-editable=\"1\" data-h=\"bed7b0b1ee\" data-kind=\"heading\" data-par=\"0\" data-ref=\"R.1 §3 ¶0\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-R.1-3-0\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §3 ¶0\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §3 ¶0 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶0</button><h2 data-body=\"1\">Review quiz</h2></div><div class=\"blk blk-quiz\" data-h=\"de5058e914\" data-kind=\"quiz\" data-par=\"1\" data-ref=\"R.1 §3 ¶1\" data-sec=\"3\" id=\"p-R.1-3-1\"><button aria-label=\"Reference R.1 §3 ¶1\" class=\"ref\" title=\"R.1 §3 ¶1 (click to copy the reference and show actions)\" type=\"button\">§3 ¶1</button><div aria-label=\"Quiz\" class=\"quiz\" data-body=\"1\" role=\"group\"><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"1\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">1.</span> You meet your teacher in the morning. What do you say?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Hello!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Goodbye!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Goodbye is for when you leave.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">Four!</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Four is a number.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"2\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">2.</span> 🖐️ How many fingers?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">three</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Count again: one, two, three, four, five.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">four</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Count again – do not forget the thumb.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">five</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"3\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">3.</span> 🟦 What colour is it?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">yellow</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Yellow is like a banana.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">blue</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">red</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">Red is like a chilli.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"4\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">4.</span> 🎒 What's this?</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a bag.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a desk.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A desk is a table.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">It's a book.</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A book has pages.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><fieldset class=\"quiz-q\" data-q=\"5\"><legend class=\"quiz-stem\"><span class=\"quiz-qn\">5.</span> 👧 A girl in your family is your…</legend><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">brother</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A brother is a boy.</div></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"1\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">sister</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span></div><div class=\"quiz-opt\" data-correct=\"0\"><label><input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\"/> <span class=\"quiz-txt\">father</span></label><span class=\"quiz-mark\"></span><div class=\"quiz-expl\" hidden=\"\">A father is a man.</div></div><div aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-result\"></div></fieldset><div class=\"quiz-actions\"><button class=\"btn btn-primary quiz-check\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-check-double\"></i> Check</button><button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary quiz-retry\" hidden=\"\" type=\"button\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa-solid fa-rotate-left\"></i> Try again</button><span aria-live=\"polite\" class=\"quiz-score\" role=\"status\"></span></div></div></div>"}], "pages": {"help": "<h1>Help</h1>\n<p>This is a <strong>review reader</strong> for <em>tli.cloud: English in Cambodia</em>. You can read every part, propose changes, propose removals and leave comments. Everything you do is saved <strong>only in this browser on this device</strong> until you export it.</p>\n<h2>Reading</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>Parts</strong> list on the left (the ☰ button on a phone) opens one part at a time.</li>\n<li>Every block has a reference in the margin, like <strong>§2 ¶3</strong>. Section 0 is the part title and the text before the first <code>##</code> heading. Each <code>##</code>/<code>###</code> heading starts a new section and is ¶0 of it. The full reference is <code>PART §section ¶paragraph</code>, for example <code>A.5 §2 ¶3</code>.</li>\n<li>Click a reference to copy it and to show the action buttons (useful on touch screens).</li>\n<li><strong>Editor notes</strong> for the open part are in the right-hand panel (below the text on small screens). They are never shown in the lesson text.</li>\n<li><strong>Search</strong> in the top bar searches all parts. Click a result to jump to the paragraph.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Editing a paragraph</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click a paragraph, heading, list item or table cell (or use the ✎ button). It turns yellow.</li>\n<li>Type your change. <strong>Enter</strong> saves (in lists Enter starts a new item; use <strong>Ctrl+Enter</strong> to save). <strong>Shift+Enter</strong> makes a line break. <strong>Esc</strong> cancels.</li>\n<li><strong>Save</strong>, <strong>Cancel</strong> or <strong>Reset to source</strong>. An edited block is marked <em>Edited</em> with a brown bar; <em>Show original</em> lets you compare.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Only one block can be edited at a time. Use <strong>Editing on/off</strong> in the top bar to read without accidental edits. Links still work with a normal click.</p>\n<p>If the source text changes after you edited it (a new build), the block shows <strong>Source changed since…</strong> and your edit is not applied. You can <em>Edit again</em> or <em>Discard</em>. The item stays in your feedback until you remove it.</p>\n<h2>Removing and commenting</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>🗑 <strong>Propose removal</strong>: the block is struck through. Click <strong>Restore</strong> to undo. The original text is recorded for the export.</li>\n<li>💬 <strong>Comment</strong>: write a note; it appears under the block with a blue bar.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>My feedback and export</h2>\n<p>The <strong>My feedback</strong> tab lists all your changes, removals and comments, grouped by part, with counts and links back to the text. Each item has <strong>Undo</strong> / <strong>Delete</strong>. <strong>Clear all</strong> asks for confirmation first.</p>\n<p>Export with <strong>Copy to clipboard</strong>, <strong>Download .md</strong> or <strong>Download .json</strong> and send the file to the editor. The Markdown export looks like this:</p>\n<pre><code># Feedback on tli.cloud: English in Cambodia\nExported 2026-11-04 14:05 · reader built 2026-11-04 12:00 · reader v1.0\nContent: 1 changes, 1 removed, 1 comments\n## A.2 Partner brief\n### A.2 §1 ¶2 — CHANGED\nBefore: \"old text\"\nAfter: \"new text\"\n### A.2 §1 ¶3 — REMOVED\nBefore: \"text\"\n- A.2 §2 ¶1 — COMMENT: my comment\n  &gt; «start of the paragraph»\n</code></pre>\n<p>Table edits are exported as a whole Markdown table; list edits as the whole list.</p>\n<h2>Images and markers (for authors)</h2>\n<p>Put an image on its own line in the Markdown:</p>\n<table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Markdown</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>![Alt text](images/x.svg)</code></td>\n<td>floats right, at most 40% wide and about 18rem high</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>![Alt text](images/x.svg){right}</code></td>\n<td>same as the default</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>![Alt text](images/x.svg){left}</code></td>\n<td>floats left</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>![Alt text](images/x.svg){full}</code></td>\n<td>full width, no float</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Two images in a row are stacked, never side by side. Headings, tables, quizzes and code always start below a floating image. On phones (narrower than 576px) nothing floats. The alt text is required: it is the caption in the lightbox and is read by screen readers.</p>\n<h2>Lightbox</h2>\n<p>Click or tap an image to enlarge it on a dark background (up to 95% of the screen; small images are enlarged up to 2×). The caption is the alt text. Close with the <strong>✕</strong> button, <strong>Esc</strong>, or a click on the dark background. Pinch-zoom works on phones.</p>\n<h2>Colour tags in tables (for authors)</h2>\n<p>End a table cell with <code>{green}</code>, <code>{yellow}</code> or <code>{red}</code>. The cell gets a colour <strong>and</strong> an icon and a hidden text (\"rated green\") so the meaning does not depend on colour alone.</p>\n<h2>Quiz syntax (for authors)</h2>\n<pre><code>```quiz\nQ: What does CEFR describe?\n- [ ] A school timetable | No: CEFR does not set timetables.\n- [x] Levels of language ability from A1 to C2\n- [ ] A Cambodian exam | No: CEFR is European and used worldwide.\n```\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Q:</code> starts a question. Each option is <code>- [ ] text | explanation</code>; mark exactly one correct option with <code>- [x]</code>.</li>\n<li>At least 3 options per question, and every wrong option needs an explanation after <code>|</code>.</li>\n<li>There is one <strong>Check</strong> button per quiz. After checking you see ✔ or ✘ per question, the explanation under a wrong answer, \"N of M correct\", \"Not answered\" for skipped questions, and <strong>Try again</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Editor notes (for authors)</h2>\n<p>Write notes for editors as an HTML comment <code>&lt;!-- … --&gt;</code> or a fenced block with the language <code>EDITOR-NOTE</code>. They are removed from the lesson text and shown in the Editor notes panel.</p>\n<h2>Privacy</h2>\n<p>Nothing is sent anywhere. Your feedback is stored in this browser's local storage; clearing browser data deletes it, so export first.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>reader v1.1 · built 2026-11-05 07:54</p>\n", "changes": "<h1>Changes</h1>\n<h2>v1.0 · 2026-11-04 · initial seed + reader</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeded parts A.1–A.7 from the planning chat with Herbert (no earlier content repository existed):\nA.1 Project overview, A.2 Partner brief (YWAM Siem Reap), A.3 Meeting agenda, A.4 Questions for the partner,\nA.5 Standards (CEFR, MoEYS and others), A.6 Glossary of abbreviations, A.7 Quiz: standards.</li>\n<li>Added the review reader v1.0 (<code>viewer/</code>), <code>check_course.py</code> and jsdom tests.</li>\n<li>Two placeholder diagrams (SVG) in <code>content/images/</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n", "openItems": "<h1>Open items</h1>\n<table class=\"table table-sm table-bordered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Part</th>\n<th>Status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Start with adults or with primary/secondary learners? Decide after the YWAM Siem Reap conversation.</td>\n<td>A.1, A.4</td>\n<td>open</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Verify the MoEYS English expectations for grades 4–6 (is A1 the target at the end of primary?).</td>\n<td>A.5</td>\n<td>open</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Confirm whether the Factory Literacy Programme is still running and whether it includes English.</td>\n<td>A.5</td>\n<td>open</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>BEEP facts (age 14+, Grade 6 completed, 624 hours, CQF level 2, 43 centres in 21 provinces) to check against the latest UNESCO/MoEYS source.</td>\n<td>A.5</td>\n<td>open</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Confirm the University of the Nations (UofN) location claim for YWAM Siem Reap.</td>\n<td>A.6</td>\n<td>open</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Check the Khmer romanisation in the glossary sample with a native speaker.</td>\n<td>A.6</td>\n<td>open</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>Replace the placeholder SVG diagrams with final artwork.</td>\n<td>A.1, A.5</td>\n<td>open</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"}, "stats": {"parts": 7, "blocks": 131, "images": 4, "quizzes": 6, "questions": 20, "notes": 6, "links_internal": 0, "links_external": 0, "cell_tags": 8}};
